# The `f1aS1` reduction of set (e)

The label-split certificate of `QED.Algebra.IBPCertSector` reduces twice the self-energy projection
`S` of the lower-loop counterterm piece `f1a_S1` (topology `f1a`)
(`QED.ThreeLoopE.SetECert.f1aS1Target`, integrals in scaleless sectors dropped) to the Kira masters
`QED.ThreeLoopE.SetECert.f1aS1Masters` of the family `QED.ThreeLoopE.SetECert.f1a`.

## Main statements

* `QED.ThreeLoopE.SetECert.f1aS1_reduction_of_den`: at every `d` with `q(d) ≠ 0`, for every family
  of values satisfying the hypotheses at `d`, the target combination equals the certified
  combination of the masters.
* `QED.ThreeLoopE.SetECert.f1aS1_reduction`: the same off a finite set of `d`.

Generated by `gen.py` (offline cache `setecert/fams`); do not edit. Integers are written as `.ofNat
n` and `.negSucc n` (`= -n - 1`).
-/

